outputs.with:
**Finding (Correctness — Blocking):** `items[0].name` dereferences index `0` unconditionally. When `items` is empty (`[]`), `items[0]` evaluates to `undefined` and throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'name')` at runtime (which TypeScript does not flag unless `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is enabled).

**Scope & Checks:** Static review of the changed line only; no project build or test suite was executed.

**Correction:**
```ts
const first: string | undefined = items[0]?.name;
```

**Regression Test:**
```ts
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

const getFirstName = (items: ReadonlyArray<{ name: string }>): string | undefined =>
  items[0]?.name;

describe("getFirstName", () => {
  it("returns undefined for an empty list instead of throwing", () => {
    expect(getFirstName([])).toBeUndefined();
  });

  it("returns the first item's name when present", () => {
    expect(getFirstName([{ name: "alpha" }, { name: "beta" }])).toBe("alpha");
  });
});
```
